Once upon a time, Prometheus77 wrote thus:
> Then the long sword (artifact or no) is blessed, rustproofed, and
> given an enchantment between +0 and +3. What I don't get then is
> the otmp->spe = max(otmp-spe, spe2) ... does this put some kind
> of cap on the enchantment?

Actually spe2 is local variable which holds possible enchantment
of +0 to +3.  The sword is generatedby mksobj() and has its own
value for enchantment in otmp->spe, which is possibly greater
than what spe2 holds.  NetHack assigns greater of the two as the
final enchantment value.

To put it succintly the generated sword always will have non-
negative enchantment and has greater chance to be +0 to +3.

